sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Client
  participant API as Auth API
  participant RL as Rate Limit
  participant Redis as Redis Bitmap And Cache
  participant OTP as Redis Forgot OTP State
  participant Mongo as MongoDB

  Client->>API: POST /auth/password/verify-otp
  API->>RL: Apply auth rate limit
  API->>API: Validate canonical email and OTP
  API->>Redis: GET bitmap:users:email:v1:ready

  alt Bitmap not ready or Redis lookup unavailable
    Note over API,Redis: Fallback to MongoDB after OTP validation
    API->>OTP: Verify forgot-password OTP
    alt OTP invalid or expired
      API-->>Client: Existing invalid or expired OTP response
    else OTP valid
      API->>Mongo: Find user by canonical email
      alt User exists
        API->>Redis: SET user:email:{hash}
        API->>Redis: SETBIT bitmap:users:email:v1
        API->>OTP: Store reset token
        API-->>Client: Reset token issued
      else User missing
        API-->>Client: Existing invalid or expired OTP response
      end
    end
  else Bitmap ready
    API->>Redis: GETBIT bitmap:users:email:v1 at email index
  end

  alt Ready and BIT = 0
    Note over API,Redis: No database lookup; keep public failure generic
    API-->>Client: Existing invalid or expired OTP response
  else Ready and BIT = 1
    Note over API,Redis: Maybe exists, OTP still controls the flow
    API->>OTP: Verify forgot-password OTP
    alt OTP invalid or expired
      API-->>Client: Existing invalid or expired OTP response
    else OTP valid
      API->>Redis: GET user:email:{sha256(email)}
      alt Positive cache hit
        API->>OTP: Store reset token
        API-->>Client: Reset token issued
      else Positive cache miss
        API->>Redis: GET nf:email:{sha256(email)}
        alt Negative cache hit
          API-->>Client: Existing invalid or expired OTP response
        else Negative cache miss
          API->>Mongo: Find user by canonical email
          alt User exists
            API->>Redis: SET user:email:{hash}
            API->>Redis: SETBIT bitmap:users:email:v1
            API->>OTP: Store reset token
            API-->>Client: Reset token issued
          else User missing
            API->>Redis: SET nf:email:{hash} EX 300
            API-->>Client: Existing invalid or expired OTP response
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
